# What never enters the build context. The image needs nothing from this
# repository's tree - no COPY line reads it, and the first_boot travels into
# the instance on its own, after the import - so everything here is either
# noise sent to the Docker daemon or a file that must not be baked into the
# image.
#
# This file sits BESIDE the Dockerfile under the name Dockerfile.dockerignore
# - the only name a builder reads next to a `-f` Dockerfile (BuildKit) - but
# its patterns are written against the CONTEXT ROOT, the repository: they
# match ./src/windows and so on, never this folder.
#
# distro/packs/ is in this list because the image carries no pack: a pack
# arrives on the instance, from Windows, and no COPY line reads that folder.
# The zsh pack carries the shell's settings the same way - the image bakes
# the tools, never a configuration.
.git
.gitattributes
.gitignore
.github
.claude
assets
docs
src/distro/packs
LICENSE
README.md
src/windows
wsl.ps1

# Build artifacts
*.tar
*.vhdx
